            "issue": "The following explicit genitive subject, τῆς κλίνης, naturally governs both coordinated participles: the cot was brought in and set down. The draft instead supplies the woman as the first participle’s subject. That contextual split attachment is defensible, but the notes discuss only ὁμῶς and do not disclose or justify this subject assignment against the more source-transparent shared-subject reading.",
